{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender global space type registry blender global space type registry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","fileName":"Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Global Space Type Registry","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Editor Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Structure","Blender SpaceType Structure","Blender Editor Registration","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender global space type registry blender global space type registry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","fileName":"Blender Global Space Type Registry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Global Space Type Registry","heading":"Blender Global Space Type Registry","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender keeps all registered [[Blender SpaceType Structure]] objects in a global linked list managed by `blenkernel`. Each space-specific setup function appends its completed runtime type through the kernel registration API.\n\nThe registry must be accessible outside the window manager because editor creation and lookup occur across several modules. [[Blender Editor Registration]] fills it once during startup, after which screen areas can match their persistent type identifiers to the runtime callbacks required for drawing, events, and construction.","tags":["baby"],"li